# What Vercel uploads when it deploys from the repository root.
#
# CLI deployments from the repository root use these rules even when the
# project's Root Directory is admin-web. Keep the upload limited to website
# files so database migrations, Flutter source and planning documents stay out.
#
# The companion piece is the root vercel.json, which rewrites incoming paths
# down into admin-web/ so the site answers on "/" rather than "/admin-web/".
#
# Git deployments with Root Directory admin-web use that directory's config.
# CLI uploads must include admin-web/vercel.json as well so hosted builds apply
# its redirects, rewrites and response headers.

# Ignore everything, then allow back only what is meant to ship.
*
!admin-web
!admin-web/**

# The deployment configuration itself. Re-included explicitly rather than
# relying on Vercel to special-case it against the `*` above.
!vercel.json

# Node test files, run with `node admin-web/tests/<file>.test.js` during
# development. No business being served to a browser.
admin-web/tests
admin-web/downloads/README.md

# Fetch the verified APK during the hosted build instead of uploading the large
# generated binary as CLI source. Partial downloads never belong in source.
admin-web/downloads/*.apk
admin-web/downloads/*.partial
